From 579bf2d08e0c1c85f9c2a14a097e91d6de7476aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:18:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] arm64: qcom: sm8450: OnePlus 10 Pro (negroni) support

Everything needed on top of upstream to build the kernel that runs on negroni,
a OnePlus 10 Pro (NE2213) used as a headless k3s node, as one commit so
it can be rebased onto newer kernels.

Base: v7.3-rc5. First exported on torvalds/linux 50d05c7c76c9 ("Merge tag
'landlock-7.3-rc3'"), the upstream commit the phone fork last merged, and
rebased without conflicts; negroni_defconfig turns CONFIG_DMABUF_DEBUG off
again, which upstream now defaults on with DEBUG_KERNEL.
Source: withsalt/linux branch 7.3-rc2 at 05e876f60a30 (Xlie Electronic
Customs' SM8450 work plus withsalt's local commits), reduced to what the
negroni build compiles, plus negroni's own battery-manager changes.

Included:
- Device tree: sm8450-oneplus-negroni.dts, the sm8450-negroni.dtso
  overlay, the fork's sm8450.dtsi changes (incl. CPU capacity and
  energy model) and the dtbs Makefile entries.
- Charging and USB-C: qcom_battmgr with the Oplus property extensions and
  the charge-limit support (qcom_battmgr_charge_limit.h), pmic_glink,
  ucsi_glink, qcom-pbs, the eUSB2 repeater and the ADSP loader
  (qcom_q6v5_pas) changes. negroni additions: CID-triggered Type-C DRP
  (BC_CID_DETECT worker), the debugfs knob qcom_battmgr/usb_prop used by
  the USB Ethernet recovery service, and reporting Oplus PD_SDP as PD
  instead of flooding the log with "enum value 17".
- SCM: "oplus,negroni" compatible.
- Display and GPU: dispcc-sm8450, the Samsung S6E3HC3 panel, DSI/DPU DSC
  fixes, Adreno 730 IFPC/GBIF settings and hang recovery.
- Touch (Synaptics S3908 oncell), TFA9872 amplifier, camss, IPA data,
  WCN6855 Bluetooth and the PCI power-sequencing fix for Wi-Fi.
- arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig: savedefconfig of the running config.

Left out (other devices in the fork, or not built for negroni): the
Kaanapali OnePlus and Xiaomi SM8550 device trees and configs, Adreno
740/830/840 changes, Kaanapali/SM8550 display clocks, the Lucid Ole PLL
change, other panels, haptics, the tri-state key, FM radio, ipa2-lite,
ath12k, oplus_battmgr and new IPCC IDs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
